  "query_preview": "..\nHOT, DRY AND BREEZY CONDITIONS SATURDAY...\n\nTonight through Sunday: \nWarm and dry conditions with generally light winds to continue\ninto tonight. Low pressure moving across British Columbia will\nusher a dry cold front into the Inland Northwest on Saturday, \nbringing a round of breezy/gusty winds. The highest winds will \nbe across the Okanogan Valley and western Columbia Basin. Wind \ngusts of 35 to 40 mph are expected at times in these areas, and \nwill be coupled with relative humidity percentages in the teens \nto low 20s. These conditions will leading to heightened fire \nweather concerns, and a Red Flag Warning is in effect for \nSaturday. The front will also bring slightly cooler temps \nthrough the weekend, though the only anticipated chances for \nprecip for the region will generally be confined to the northern\nID panhandle on Sunday. \n\nMonday through Friday: A high pressure ridge is expected for\nmuch of next week. Warm and dry conditions to persist, with\ndaytime temps climbing into the upper 80s and 90s. Wednesday \nhas breezy winds through the Cascade Gaps with a weak and quick-\nmoving disturbance pushing through the region. Toward the end \nof the week (starting around Friday), models start to diverge\nmore substantially. Something to watch in a case a pattern \nshift becomes more likely. /KD",
